00:00:05.120 --> 00:00:08.660
 

00:00:08.660 --> 00:00:11.419
Hello and welcome to KnowledgeHut

00:00:11.419 --> 00:00:15.750
Building a product successfully doesn’t
mean building a successful product.

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:19.950
Building a product successfully doesn’t
create value for the customer, but building

00:00:19.950 --> 00:00:22.420
a successful product does.

00:00:22.420 --> 00:00:27.430
Therefore it is logical to aim at building
a successful product instead of aiming to

00:00:27.430 --> 00:00:29.680
build a product successfully.

00:00:29.680 --> 00:00:35.750
But before the arrival of Agile Manifesto,
this was not the case in the software industry.

00:00:35.750 --> 00:00:40.780
Software development was being done by following
a rigid process, a lot of importance was given

00:00:40.780 --> 00:00:46.300
to documentation, developers cared only about
following the contracts instead of caring

00:00:46.300 --> 00:00:49.200
about delivering a useful product.

00:00:49.200 --> 00:00:54.899
As the complexities of the products kept increasing,
so did the delivery time, what was being delivered

00:00:54.899 --> 00:01:00.130
was not meeting customer expectations and
products were failing at a rapid rate.

00:01:00.130 --> 00:01:05.860
Then in 2001, 17 software developers came
together to discuss possible lightweight methods

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:07.660
for software development.

00:01:07.660 --> 00:01:12.940
They came up with a manifesto which had 4
values and 12 principles to make the software

00:01:12.940 --> 00:01:15.580
development process more agile.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:19.680
This manifesto is known as the Agile Manifesto.

00:01:19.680 --> 00:01:24.500
These values and principles brought tremendous
improvements in the software development process

00:01:24.500 --> 00:01:28.941
and now they are even being followed for the
development of non-software products, such

00:01:28.941 --> 00:01:35.049
as computers, motor vehicles, medical devices,
food, clothing, and music etc.

00:01:35.049 --> 00:01:40.640
In this video, we will be discussing the four
values given in the Agile manifesto one by one.

00:01:40.640 --> 00:01:45.000
Individuals and interactions over process
and tools.

00:01:45.770 --> 00:01:49.950
During the time of Waterfall method, a lot
of attention was given to the processes being

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:50.950
followed.

00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:56.869
Waterfall method itself was a 5 step process
which had to be followed in order to develop software.

00:01:57.869 --> 00:02:02.250
Following stringent processes used to make
the development process rigid and changes

00:02:02.250 --> 00:02:05.250
could not be brought easily when required.

00:02:05.250 --> 00:02:10.450
Additionally, a well-defined process is not
the answer to every problem.

00:02:10.450 --> 00:02:15.620
No matter how detailed and well defined a
process is, there will always come some barriers

00:02:15.620 --> 00:02:19.530
which couldn’t have been anticipated by
any process or tool.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:24.530
Such barriers are overcome when individuals
sit together, discuss and find the solution

00:02:24.530 --> 00:02:25.840
of the problems.

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:31.760
Also, innovation doesn’t come from rigid
processes but it comes from free minds.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:36.540
This is why the Agile Manifesto says that
we should focus more on having competent people

00:02:36.540 --> 00:02:38.930
working together effectively.

00:02:38.930 --> 00:02:43.690
Process and tools should be used but only
until they are making things easy and effective

00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:45.140
for us.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:48.270
Working software over comprehensive documents.

00:02:48.270 --> 00:02:52.210
The Waterfall method used to start with heavy
documentation process.

00:02:52.210 --> 00:02:57.220
A lot of documentation used to be done before
even starting to build the software.

00:02:57.220 --> 00:03:03.360
The features, specifications, layouts, requirements,
test cases etc were documented long before

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:05.069
their arrival time.

00:03:05.069 --> 00:03:09.520
This approach had some drawbacks like, what
you have documented will be outdated by the

00:03:09.520 --> 00:03:13.740
time you are done with it, you may end up
creating many features which may never be

00:03:13.740 --> 00:03:19.340
used by the end user, the time spent on the
documentation of such features also goes in

00:03:19.340 --> 00:03:20.390
vain.

00:03:20.390 --> 00:03:25.599
Too much documentation also delays the project
which later becomes an opportunity cost for

00:03:25.599 --> 00:03:26.880
the business.

00:03:26.880 --> 00:03:32.790
Because of all these drawbacks, Agile Manifesto
favors working software over comprehensive

00:03:32.790 --> 00:03:33.790
documents.

00:03:33.790 --> 00:03:38.000
Instead of wasting a lot of time in creating
long documents and then taking feedbacks on

00:03:38.000 --> 00:03:43.650
the basis of those documents, we should take
the feedback on the basis of working software.

00:03:43.650 --> 00:03:49.310
A basic software with all the basic features
should be created first and then it should

00:03:49.310 --> 00:03:54.390
be given to the end users and stakeholders,
then on the basis of the feedback received

00:03:54.390 --> 00:03:58.230
from the users, further development should
be carried out.

00:03:58.230 --> 00:04:03.230
In this way a lot of time is saved, also,
the created software has the features which

00:04:03.230 --> 00:04:05.780
provide value to the end users

00:04:05.780 --> 00:04:12.680
Customer collaboration over contract negotiation
In the traditional method of software development,

00:04:12.680 --> 00:04:17.720
the customer was involved only at the beginning
of the project for contract negotiation, one

00:04:17.720 --> 00:04:22.319
more time if there are any changes to be made
in the contract and finally at the end of

00:04:22.319 --> 00:04:23.669
the project.

00:04:23.669 --> 00:04:28.139
The development process was more focussed
on what is written in the contract instead

00:04:28.139 --> 00:04:31.330
of being focused on what the customer wants.

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:35.879
This approach neglected the value of customer
feedback during the project.

00:04:35.879 --> 00:04:40.729
When software is developed without the constant
feedback of the customer, the end result is

00:04:40.729 --> 00:04:45.669
often a product which does not satisfy the
needs of the customers completely.

00:04:45.669 --> 00:04:51.729
This is why the Agile Manifesto favours customer
collaboration over contract negotiation.

00:04:51.729 --> 00:04:56.169
Agile emphasises on taking constant feedbacks
from the customer throughout the development

00:04:56.169 --> 00:05:01.879
process so that whatever is being developed
is also being seen by the customer.

00:05:01.879 --> 00:05:06.020
Whenever the customer feels that the project
is going in the wrong direction then he or

00:05:06.020 --> 00:05:10.949
she can steer the project by providing inputs
to the developers.

00:05:10.949 --> 00:05:16.089
Respond to change over following plan
Traditional software development methods were

00:05:16.089 --> 00:05:18.199
not in the favour of change.

00:05:18.199 --> 00:05:23.099
The traditional approach was to create detailed
plans in the beginning and then following

00:05:23.099 --> 00:05:25.020
them throughout the project.

00:05:25.020 --> 00:05:30.449
Being rigid does not only lead to the creation
of an improper product but it also makes us

00:05:30.449 --> 00:05:34.899
miss the chances of bringing changes which
could make our product better.

00:05:34.899 --> 00:05:40.569
This is why Agile manifesto favours responding
to change over following plans.

00:05:40.569 --> 00:05:45.689
When software is developed with agility we
start with a plan which give us enough idea

00:05:45.689 --> 00:05:48.479
of the direction towards we want to move.

00:05:48.479 --> 00:05:53.779
Then as we proceed and see new events unfolding
in front of us we incorporate those realities

00:05:53.779 --> 00:05:55.770
into the ongoing work.

00:05:55.770 --> 00:06:00.969
New events are nots seen as obstacles but
anything new in our way becomes an opportunity

00:06:00.969 --> 00:06:03.789
for us to provide additional value.

00:06:03.789 --> 00:06:07.429
So these were the four values of Agile Manifesto.

00:06:07.429 --> 00:06:10.800
Follow them in your project management to
ensure its success.

00:06:10.800 --> 00:06:15.809
Don’t forget to subscribe knowledgehut and
visit our website for Agile related trainings.

